From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Paul=20B=C3=BCchner?=
 <45827409+paulbuechner@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:54:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vtkRenderWindow: Reverse Z where depth is computed, compared
 or converted

UseReverseZ reversed the depth of the polygon mappers, the camera and
the renderer's conversions. Everything that writes, clears, compares or
converts depth itself kept the conventional range, so with reverse Z on
it drew wrong or not at all: 2-D actors at NDC z -1 fell outside the
[0, 1] clip range and vanished, impostor spheres and tubes, the sphere
and stick mappers and the volumes wrote conventional depth, translucent
passes peeled in the wrong order, and pickers took the farthest depth
for the nearest.

Each of them now follows the window's UseReverseZ, read when it renders
(a uniform, or a bit in the polydata mapper's shader-change value where
the convention is part of a shader's source):
- mappers: points as spheres and lines as tubes (both polydata mappers),
  the sphere and stick mappers, the low-memory mapper's coincident
  topology, the labeled mappers' offsets, 2-D actors (foreground at NDC
  1, background at 0), the skybox and the fluid mapper;
- passes: depth peeling and dual depth peeling, order-independent
  translucency, SSAO, eye-dome lighting, depth of field, point fill, the
  shadow-map baker, the value pass and vtkClearZPass;
- pickers and widgets: vtkRenderer::GetZ and PickProp, the hardware
  selector, vtkWorldPointPicker, vtkSelectVisiblePoints, vtkAreaPicker,
  the 3-D point pickers and the representations that build rays or
  place props on the near plane;
- volumes: the GPU ray cast mapper's depth conversions, termination and
  written depth, projected tetrahedra, and the CPU ray cast and sweep
  mappers.

Passes that work on conventional depth formulas (dual depth peeling,
SSAO, EDL, depth of field, point fill, the shadow baker, the CPU volume
mappers) take 1 - depth: correct, at conventional precision. No member
is added; behaviour without reverse Z is unchanged.
